<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Canberra confirms Qantas-JAL codeshare.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Canberra confirms Qantas-JAL codeshare.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's International Air Services Commission said it confirmed its earlier draft approval of Qantas Airways Ltd and Japan Airlines Co Ltd codesharing their Tokyo flights to Brisbane and Cairns.</p>
<p>&quot;The commision's decision (will) enable Qantas to offer daily non-stop services between Brisbane and Tokyo while continuing to offer daily services between Cairns and Tokyo,&quot; said the commission, which authorises Australia's international air services.  </p>
<p>&quot;Most of the flights to and from Brisbane (will) be operated by Japan Airlines, while the flights to and from Cairns (will) be operated by Qantas.&quot;</p>
<p>Codesharing allows one airline to sell seats on another's flights as if they were its own.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
